{"created": "2026-10-22T03:23:26.065211+00:00", "modified": "2026-10-22T03:23:26.861614+00:00", "id": 23552014, "conceptrecid": "23552013", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.23552014", "conceptdoi": "10.5281/zenodo.23552013", "doi_url": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23552014", "metadata": {"title": "A circulant Ramsey (3,33)-graph on 240 vertices: R(3,33) >= 241 and R(3,34) >= 244", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.23552014", "publication_date": "2026-10-22", "description": "<p>Certificate and independent checkers for new lower bounds on classical Ramsey numbers. The circulant graph Cay(Z_240, &plusmn;{14, 34, 38, 40, 43, 50, 58, 60, 63, 67, 69, 70, 79, 87, 89, 99}) is triangle-free with independence number 32, so R(3,33) &gt;= 241 (previous best 230, arXiv:2608.18769). With the Burr&ndash;Erd\u0151s&ndash;Faudree&ndash;Schelp inequality this gives R(3,34) &gt;= 244 (previous best 239). The bound alpha &lt;= 32 was verified by three separately written exact solvers using orbital branching. Reproduction instructions are in README.md. The search code and certificate were developed with Claude Code (Anthropic), an AI coding agent, in a project directed by the author.</p>", "access_right": "open", "creators": [{"name": "Suresh Kannan, Satyajeeth", "affiliation": null}], "keywords": ["ramsey numbers", "R(3, k)", "circulant graphs", "Cayley graphs", "triangle-free graphs", "independence number"], "related_identifiers": [{"identifier": "arXiv:2608.18769", "relation": "references", "resource_type": "publication-workingpaper", "scheme": "arxiv"}], "version": "1.0", "language": "eng", "custom": {"code:programmingLanguage": [{"id": "python", "title": {"en": "Python"}}, {"id": "c", "title": {"en": "C"}}]}, "resource_type": {"title": "Dataset", "type": "dataset"}, "license": {"id": "cc-by-4.0"}, "relations": {"version": [{"index": 0, "is_last": true, "parent": {"pid_type": "recid", "pid_value": "23552013"}}]}}, "title": "A circulant Ramsey (3,33)-graph on 240 vertices: R(3,33) >= 241 and R(3,34) >